        unspecified-site code no anatomical site is lost; the only specificity loss is
        infection/inflammation -> any complication. Moderate tier: parent crosswalk verified in Athena,
        target is meaningfully broader on the complication axis but site is preserved by the source
        being unspecified.
        """
}
mapping "T848A.1" source="T848A" target="473038008" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source T848A = Swedish subcode of ICD-10 T84.8 SNOMED CT 473038008, localized to cervical spine.
        T84.8 has Athena edge to SNOMED CT 43021250 (Complication associated with orthopedic device,
        concept_code 473038008). The Swedish A-K/X suffix encodes body region only; no region-specific
        SNOMED CT concept exists. Target subsumes the source (broader); moderate confidence because the
        crosswalk is at the parent T84.8 level, not independently re-verified for the Swedish extension.
        """
}
mapping "T848B.1" source="T848B" target="473038008" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source T848B = Swedish subcode of T84.8 (other complication of internal orthopedic prosthetic
        devices/implants/grafts), localized to shoulder/upper arm. Same reasoning as T848A: T84.8
        Athena-maps to SNOMED CT 43021250 (Complication associated with orthopedic device). Region detail
        is not representable; broader mapping to the parent SNOMED CT concept. Moderate confidence.
        """
}
